   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the town law and the public officers law, in relation to authorizing town justices in the town of Benson, in the county of Hamilton, to reside outside such town",
    "basePrintNo": "S5475",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5475-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §23, Town L; amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Town Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5475\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the town law and the public officers law, in relation to\nauthorizing town justices in the town of Benson, in the county of\nHamilton, to reside outside such town\n\nPURPOSE:\nThis bill will authorize the Town of Benson, in the county of\nHamilton, to utilize town justices who reside outside the Town of\nBenson.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nNew York State Town Law is amended such that\nthe town justice of the Town of Benson, in Hamilton County, need not\nreside in the Town of Benson.\n\nSection 2 states that a person residing outside the Town of Benson in\nHamilton County, in an adjoining town, shall not be prevented from\nholding the position of town justice in the Town of Benson.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThis legislation will allow the Town of Benson to\nselect the most qualified person to be the Town Justice of the Town\nof Benson, regardless of his, or her residency status. Without this\nlegislation the Town of Benson would be limited to only being able to\nchoose a town justice from within the Town of Benson itself.\n\nThis legislation has been requested by the Town of Benson.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
